xnu 0350: the panel copy waits for the frame it copies

Nothing on this port waits for the submission that named a surface. The GL
interposer skips its glFinish (a full sync puts the CPU behind the GPU and the
display drops to about twenty swaps a second, docs/COREANIMATION_GLES.md) and
the display driver never looked at the fence, so `swap()` copies the canvas
while the GPU may still be drawing it. On the glass that is a frame with pieces
of the previous one in it -- the diagonal stair edges of a raster in flight,
black where nothing has been written yet -- and it stays there until something
redraws, because CoreAnimation only draws on change.

`mondrian_gpu_retire()` waits, bounded at 100 ms, for the fence the submission
path already handed out; the framebuffer calls it once per present, before the
layer loop, behind `mondrianfb_gpuwait=1` for an A/B. It does not consume the
fence, so `gpuacct`'s numbers stay the client's, and it is not a glFinish: the
wait sits in the present thread, on the GPU's own remaining time, instead of
serialising the renderer's CPU work behind the GPU.

The fps line now reports `gpuwait avg`, which is what that wait costs.
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
@@ -5676,6 +5676,43 @@
 	mondrian_log_flush_now();
 }
 
+/*
+ * Wait until everything the compositor has submitted so far has retired.
+ *
+ * The framebuffer calls this before it copies a surface into the panel, and
+ * nothing else guarantees it: the GL interposer does not glFinish at the end of
+ * a frame (a full sync puts the CPU behind the GPU and the display drops to
+ * about twenty swaps a second), and the display driver never looked at the
+ * fence. A copy taken from a surface the GPU is still drawing is a frame with
+ * pieces of the previous one on the glass -- the diagonal stair edges of a
+ * raster in flight -- and the glass keeps it until something redraws.
+ *
+ * The wait is bounded and does not consume the fence: it is the one the
+ * submission path already handed out, so `gpuacct`'s numbers stay the client's.
+ */
+int
+mondrian_gpu_retire(void)
+{
+	volatile uint32_t *view = (volatile uint32_t *)mondrian_cp_memptr_view;
+	uint32_t fence = mondrian_uc_fence;
+	uint32_t spent_us = 0;
+
+	if (view == NULL || fence == 0) {
+		return -1;
+	}
+	for (;;) {
+		__asm__ volatile("dsb sy" ::: "memory");
+		if ((int32_t)(view[mondrian_uc_fence_word(fence)] - fence) >= 0) {
+			return 0;
+		}
+		if (spent_us >= 100000u) {
+			return -1;
+		}
+		delay(50);
+		spent_us += 50u;
+	}
+}
+
 int
 mondrian_gpu_uc_wait(uint32_t fence, uint32_t timeout_ms)
 {
